{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>These are the generations of Shem.</b> You will not find mention of death in the generations of Shem as you find in the earlier generations from Adam to Noah. And it is possible that there is a reason for this, because the kingship of the house of David comes from Shem, and Mashiach ben David will have no death in him, but is destined to live forever; for from the time of his coming it will be 837 years to the completion of the sixth millennium, which is the numerical value of (Isaiah 9:6) ״לםרבה המשרה״ — for the count of the closed mem is 400, and after 837 he will enter immediately into the seventh millennium, which is entirely sabbath and eternal life; and concerning him David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 21:4): ״חיים שאל ממך נתתה לו אורך ימים עולם ועד״. Moreover, the gentiles do not merit the resurrection of the dead — only we, the children of Shem; and Scripture said of the gentiles that each of them shall go in the name of their elohim, as it is written (Micah 4:5): ״כי כל העמים ילכו איש בשם אלהיו ואנחנו נלך בשם ה׳ אלהינו לעולם ועד״, and it is written of Israel (Deuteronomy 4:4): ״ואתם הדבקים בה׳ אלהיכם חיים כלכם היום״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The gematria explanation is rendered exactly as written: the value of לםרבה המשרה with a closed mem is given as 400 for the mem (rather than the open mem's 40), plus 837 years — copied digit-for-digit without verification."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:11:40.150848165Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}